  "reason": "Rejected: although the recovered raster has clean transparency, correct N/S placement, and a broadly Heartlands-consistent warm-loam palette, its alpha>=240 route band measures only 25/25/12 px on the N arm and 23/25/13 px on the S arm at the required 50/75/100% samples, below the required constant 32-36 px total band and necessarily below the 28 px loam-core minimum. Both terminal cross-sections taper sharply, and the raster contains no required sub-240 6-10 px irregular verge feather, so the four-neighbor seam remains pinched and the candidate cannot be approved.",
